dcomp, winewayland: a window-hosted WebView2 shows its page.

FL Studio 2026's Browser > SOUNDS tab (WebView2 154) stayed empty, and any app hosting WebView2 in a window
showed nothing (lab, 2026-11-03, with a minimal WebView2 host as well). Four steps, each measured:

1. DCompositionCreateDevice(IID_IDCompositionDevice) answered E_NOINTERFACE; we had only the desktop
   device. Chromium's software output (OutputDeviceBacking) CHECKs that call, so the GPU process crashed
   six times and the browser quit ("GPU process isn't usable. Goodbye."). The device now answers the
   original IDCompositionDevice by forwarding to the same implementation, as Windows' device does.
2. register_presentation: Chromium's GPU process presents into its own "Intermediate D3D Window", a child
   of the browser process's window, inside the host app's window. Its pixels live in the HOST's
   window_surface, but the bridge took it for same-process and blitted into a detached DC. A target whose
   top-level window belongs to another process is now cross-process (shared-memory path). Reached only
   when no CEF panel host matched, so the CEP paths are unchanged.
3. dcomp_register_external: a composition swapchain Presents with no window, and every frame went to the
   pending hwnd -- DXVK's hidden 320x240 DXVKDUMMYWINDOW. A Present on a swapchain that a committed visual
   already registered now marks that presentation. The visual holds DXVK's DxgiSwapChainDispatcher and the
   Present reports the DxgiSwapChain inside it; ID3DDestructionNotifier, which the dispatcher forwards, names
   the same object from both. The pending-hwnd fallback stays for swapchains no visual registered.
4. The readback took GetBuffer(0). After a flip-model Present that is the NEXT back buffer, the frame from
   BufferCount presents ago, never drawn after a first Present; the presented frame is the last buffer
   (DXGI's read-only front buffer; DXVK's RotateBackBuffers moves it there). A static page presents once,
   so it never showed. The readback now takes the presented frame, which is what DWM shows.
winewayland: the present consumer also presents registered windows of another process whose top-level
window is ours (step 2's window, presented by the host app's consumer).

Lab, minimal WebView2 host on 11.10-173 + this, page with a counter: page shown and updating, 2 of 2 runs;
without 2-4 (173d) the window stayed grey. With dxvk 0005 / dxvk-dxgi 0003 every frame is whole. Needs
dxgi.enableDummyCompositionSwapchain = True for msedgewebview2.exe (without it CreateSwapChainForComposition
is E_NOTIMPL and the GPU process restarts in a loop).

--- a/dlls/dcomp/device.c
+++ b/dlls/dcomp/device.c
@@ -47,6 +47,11 @@
